## Training requirements

1. Load a documented dataset.
2. Validate the required columns.
3. Handle missing values without leaking test information.
4. Convert timestamps and units consistently.
5. Sort time-dependent records chronologically.
6. Define the prediction target and features explicitly.
7. Use a chronological train/test split for time-series data.
8. Establish a simple baseline.
9. Train a Random Forest Regressor.
10. Evaluate both models on the same held-out test period.
11. Save the fitted preprocessing pipeline and model.
12. Save the feature schema, training timestamp, data range, and metrics.
13. Provide reproducible training commands.
14. Reject incompatible prediction inputs.
15. Detect model and feature-schema mismatches.

Avoid target leakage.

If lag features are used, create them in chronological order and ensure that only information available at prediction time is used.

If the dataset is too small or unsuitable, display a clear explanation and do not claim the model is reliable.

